    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνιπτόπους</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with unwashen feet,</i>
			epith. of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σελλοί,</span> Dodonaean
			priests of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.235
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				7.276
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lydia</span>); applied to parasites by
				<i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				139
			</span></i>; to the Great Bear, as <i>metuens aequore tingi,</i> by
				<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				40.285
			</span></i>.</div>
